{\b VR Gaze Mirror \emdash  unofficial community build}\par
\par
This package mirrors your VR view for OBS and window capture, and draws a ring on that mirror where you are looking. The ring is never visible in the headset.\par
\par
Everything it installs is this project's own code (MIT licence):\par
\par
\bullet  {\b The gaze mirror layer} \emdash  an OpenXR API layer that makes the mirror picture for OpenXR games.\par
\bullet  {\b The SteamVR helper} \emdash  makes the mirror picture for games that use SteamVR directly. It uses Valve's OpenVR library (BSD licence).\par
\bullet  {\b The "Gaze Mirror" OBS plugin} \emdash  shows the picture in OBS (GPL-2, as OBS plugins are).\par
\bullet  {\b The mirror window and the settings app.}\par
\par
Nothing third-party is modified. {\b Quad-Views-Foveated} by Matthieu Bucchianeri (MIT licence) is optional: it gives foveated rendering and is not needed for the ring. His official, unmodified 1.1.3 installer is shipped with this package and offered on the last page when it is not installed. He did not build, test or endorse this package; please do not ask him for support with it.\par
\par
Upgrading from 1.x removes the modified layers and the "OpenXR Mirror Capture" OBS plugin that 1.x installed. Replace that source in your OBS scenes with the new "Gaze Mirror" source.\par
\par
This package is not code-signed. Games that use anti-cheat software may refuse to load the layer.\par
\par
The full licence texts are installed in the Licences folder next to the app.\par
